with over two dozen different marvel  movies and more than a few marvel  television shows  we've seen some incredible comic  book-based performances from some of  hollywood's very best actors  not all of those actors are still with  us but thankfully they've left behind a  long and impressive body of work  even beyond their marvel roles here are  marvel actors you may not know  passed away powers booth  if you don't recognize power's booth  from his brief appearance in the  avengers  or his run on marvel's agents of shield  you probably know him as cult leader jim  jones in guyana tragedy  a role that won him an emmy you may also  know him as the conniving brothel owner  cy toliver on hbo's deadwood or as 24's  vice president noah daniels  marvel fans however will always see  booth as gideon malik the shadowy world  leader that was first seen in the  avengers where he encouraged nick fury  to nuke new york city in order to stop  loki's alien army malek later returned  for marvel's agents of shield  as season three's big bad and the head  of hydra  you have less than 15 minutes to breach  their barricades and regain control of  that chamber  sir soldier malik isn't the only comic  book character that booth played either  he voiced guerrilla grodd and red  tornado in justice league unlimited  played lex luthor in the animated  feature superman brainiac attacks  and appeared in both sin city movies as  senator rourke  sadly booth passed away in may 2017.  on-screen villainy will never be the  same  roy scheider when a group of thugs show  up at the castle family reunion looking  to exact revenge in 2004 as the punisher  roy scheider's frank castle senior is  there to stop them  in their tracks  not that you'd expect anything less from  the man who faced down jaws not once  but twice and live to tell the story as  police chief martin brody  scheider is one of the three men who  take to the seas in order to stop the  tourist eating great white  reportedly scheider even improvised  brody's most famous line  [Music]  you're gonna need a bigger boat he left  behind an impressive resume beyond jaws  though he received an academy award  nomination for playing grizzled  detective cloudy russo in the french  connection and another for his role in  all that jazz  scheider passed away in 2008  gary shandling in iron man 2  gary shandling's senator stern tries to  discredit iron man  and transfer tony stark's tech for the  united states government but the extent  of his villainy becomes even more  established in captain america the  winter soldier  it's one of the most memorable parts of  marvel movie history but it's barely a  footnote in shandling's long and  accomplished career  chandling started his career as a writer  for 70 sitcoms  but decided to pursue stand-up comedy  appearances on the tonight show landed  channeling a gig as one of johnny  carson's go-to guest hosts  and eventually led to the subversive  fourth wall breaking sitcom it's gary  shandling show  later chandling funneled his tonight  show experience into the larry sanders  show  an hbo series about a late night talk  show over the course of its six season  run  the larry sanders show amassed a  whopping 56  emmy nominations helped make jeffrey  tambor rip torn and janine garofalo into  household names  and cemented its place as one of the  greatest television shows ever made  unfortunately chandling passed away in  2016.  bill paxton fan favorite character actor  bill paxton  added a helpful dose of star power to  marvel's agents of shield when he  brought the cyborg assassin  john garrett to life on screen for the  very first time in 2014.  why do i hear gunfire you hear the dying  breath of an old world general  but a new world is coming i've tasted it  on my tongue  as garrett paxton lured straight-laced  shield agent grant ward to the dark  side uncovered the secret behind phil  coulson's mysterious resurrection  and ultimately ended up on the wrong  side of coulson's disintegration gun  unfortunately paxton who made his name  as a scene-stealing presence in classic  movies like aliens  terminator edge of tomorrow true lies  and many many others  passed away just a few years later due  to complications resulting from heart  surgery  neil fingleton a british athlete turned  actor who stood  at a record setting seven feet seven  inches tall  neil fingleton was officially the  tallest man in britain he played college  basketball at the university of north  carolina  and college of the holy cross  represented britain in the world  university games and later played  professionally  in boston italy spain and greece however  fingleton's sports career came to an  abrupt end in 2007  when an injury finished his time on the  court he turned to acting  where his massive size landed him all  kinds of unique roles  in doctor who fingleton appeared  opposite peter capaldi  as the would-be conqueror fisher king he  also played game of thrones resident  giant  mag the mighty on the marvel side  fingleton actually played two roles  fingelton helped bring ultron to life  working as both a stunned performer  and motion capture artist on avengers  age of ultron  he also played a russian bodyguard in  x-men first class  he died of heart failure in february of  2017.  cliff robertson compared to the rest of  the cast in spider-man  cliff robertson's uncle ben might not  have the most screen time  but it's his teachings that ultimately  inspire peter parker to become  spider-man  remember with great power comes great  responsibility  much like ben robertson was a real life  hero  while he stole hearts as a young john f  kennedy in pt 109  and won an oscar for the lead role in  charlie he's  probably best known for taking a stand  against hollywood corruption  in 1977 robertson reported that columbia  pictures head david begelman had forged  his name on a ten thousand dollar check  as part of a massive embezzling scheme  in the aftermath  begelman lost his job and hollywood  bigwigs refused to give robertson more  parts  robertson never fully embraced the show  business machine and he wasn't sorry for  his actions shining a light on hollywood  corruption  robertson passed away in 2011. harry  dean stanton  if you don't know harry dean stanton's  name you certainly know his face  in the 60s and 70s he slowly emerged as  one of hollywood's most reliable  character actors  thanks to memorable bit parts in films  and television shows like cool hand luke  gunsmoke and the godfather part 2.  stanton's popularity eventually led to  bigger supporting roles  including parts in alien escape from new  york and the green mile  in 1984 he took the lead in the  critically acclaimed paris texas  and the same year he co-starred his bud  in the cult classic sci-fi romp  repo man he's also notable for playing a  recurring part in twin peaks to return  his second to last project before his  september 2017  passing in between his pack schedule  stanton found time to sneak into the  marvel cinematic universe  with a scene stealing performance as a  wise janitor in the avengers  i'm out of space an alien  well then son you've got a condition  eugenie eugene lazarus in the marvel  cinematic universe  anton vanco was a longtime stark  industries employee who helped develop  the ark reactor before being found  guilty of espionage  and shipped back to russia after a  lengthy stint in siberia ivanko returned  to civilization to raise his son  turning ivan vonko against the starks  and creating iron man 2's main villain  whiplash thankfully the actor who played  banco  euv guinea eugene lazarus wasn't quite  so twisted in real life  a russian native lazariff was a  well-known and accomplished actor in his  motherland  where he was honored with the people's  artist of russia title the most  prestigious government award  a russian performer can attain on his  move to the united states  lazarus kept right on acting appearing  in films and tv shows like the pink  panther 2  24 alias the west wing lord of war and  many others  he didn't keep all of that experience to  himself either  between roles lazarus taught acting at  the university of southern california  sadly he died of a heart attack in 2016.  michael clark duncan when you're casting  someone like new york crime boss  wilson fisk better known to superhero  fans as kingpin  you need someone who's got a huge  presence michael clark duncan didn't  just look the part with his six foot 300  pound frame  he also had charisma to spare the  actor's stature helped him land the gig  as the big bad in 2003's daredevil  have you seen the papers today  somebody's been talking  [Music]  somebody always does duncan a superhero  fan since childhood was very  enthusiastic about playing fisk  he re-read frank miller's comic book run  from front to back before filming  daredevil  and returned to voice the character in  spider-man the new animated series  still the kingpin was just one of many  memorable parts duncan played over the  years  duncan appeared in films like armageddon  the whole nine yards  sin city and others usually playing  criminals or other heavies  but his star making turn came in 1999  when he joined the cast of frank  darabont's the green mile  duncan landed the role as the imposing  but gentle inmate john coffey  and was rewarded for his efforts with a  handful of award nominations  including one for best supporting actor  duncan passed away from a heart attack  in september 2012. bill bixby  visit any reasonably sized comic book  convention and you'll find that lou  ferrigno  the six foot five bodybuilder who played  marvel's jade giant on the 1977  incredible hulk television show  is live well and still signing  autographs for adoring fans  unfortunately his on-screen alter ego  bill bixby  is no longer with us bixby will always  be best known for his portrayal of david  bruce banner  the heroic scientist who traveled the  country in search of a cure for his  condition mr mcgee  don't make me angry you wouldn't like me  when i'm angry  even without the marvel bonafides he'd  be well remembered  in 1971 he was nominated for a best  actor emmy for his ongoing role in the  courtship of eddie's father  and followed that up in 1976 with two  more emmy nods  he was an accomplished director helming  30 episodes of blossom  as well as other television shows  bixby's showmanship extended off-screen  too he performed all of his own tricks  while starring in nbc's the magician  sadly bixby passed away in 1993 after a  two-year battle with cancer
 

